# ~/.claude/state/agents.local  (host-local; gitignored, copy this, drop ".example")
#
# Host-local INSTANCE launchd agents: the standalone-agent analogue of the host-local paths.env.
# launchd/install-agents.sh discovers this file GENERICALLY and renders each line into a
# com.<ns>.<job> launchd agent. The published core names none of these instances.
# The codename lives only here, on the host that runs it.
#
# Format (one agent per line):  job|role|exec-args|schedule|marker
#   job        label suffix → com.organism.<job>
#   role     ∈ per_host | singleton_bookkeeping | singleton_sideeffect   (role.py gates it)
#   exec-args  command after run.sh; may use $HOOKS (deployed hooks dir) and $HOME.
#              Whitespace-split into argv with globbing disabled: one token = one argv entry,
#              no quoting, a token can NEVER contain a space, so a path with a space in it
#              cannot be an arg.
#   schedule ∈ keepalive | interval:<sec> | cal:<H>:<M> | calw:<weekday>:<H>:<M>
#              An unrecognized token is skipped with a ⚠️ warning, the agent is NOT (re)rendered
#              and any existing plist is left untouched.
#   marker     OPTIONAL 5th field: the state/<marker>-last-success file this job writes on
#              success. A 4-field line still parses, it just declares no marker.
#              `install-agents.sh --freshness` derives the reconciler's freshness watch from
#              these declarations, so a retired job leaves the watch by deleting its line.
#              It is NOT always the job name: several jobs may share one marker (two
#              instances of one script; a job and its --fallback partner). Declare only what
#              the code ACTUALLY writes, a job that never calls jobstatus.mark_success()
#              must leave this blank, or it reports "(never)" forever and means nothing.
# Blank lines and #comments are ignored (leading whitespace tolerated).
#
# Example, a personal report kept under the gitignored hooks/local/ dir, run daily at 07:45:
# myreport|singleton_bookkeeping|python3 $HOOKS/local/myreport.py|cal:7:45|myreport
